#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= Ground Transportation & Rail

== Rail Travel

Rail transit is the preferred and environmentally responsible option for journeys under four (4) hours between connected metropolitan areas.

#policy-rule("POL-GRN-001", "Rail Travel Standards")[
  Standard Second Class (Economy) rail tickets are standard. First Class rail travel is reimbursable only for continuous journeys exceeding four (4) hours or where productive business work requiring quiet workspace has been pre-approved by the department manager.
]

== Public Transit, Taxis & Ride-Hailing

Employees are encouraged to utilize public transit (subway, metro, commuter rail) whenever safe and practical.

#policy-rule("POL-GRN-002", "Taxis and Ride-Hailing Services")[
  Taxis and rideshare services (e.g., Uber, Lyft, FreeNow) are allowable when public transit is impractical, when carrying heavy presentation equipment, or when traveling late at night (after 21:00) for personal safety. Premium service tiers (Uber Black, Lyft Lux, Executive VIP) are strictly prohibited.
]

== Rental Vehicles

Car rentals should only be booked when public transit, rail, or rideshare services are unavailable or demonstrably less economical.

#policy-rule("POL-GRN-003", "Rental Vehicle Class and Fuel")[
  Rental cars must be booked in the Compact or Intermediate class. Full-size, SUV, and Luxury rentals require advance Director approval. Vehicles must be refueled prior to return to avoid excessive vendor refueling surcharges.
]

== Personal Vehicle Mileage

Employees utilizing personal vehicles for approved business journeys are reimbursed on a standard distance rate.

#policy-rule("POL-GRN-004", "Mileage Reimbursement Rate")[
  Business mileage in personal vehicles is reimbursed at €0.38 per kilometer in the European Union and \$0.67 per mile in the United States. This rate covers all fuel, maintenance, insurance, and vehicle depreciation. Normal commuting from home to the designated primary work office is strictly non-reimbursable.
]
